1 :- Foundation what the chart ruler actually is
find the rising sign first.
then identify its ruler using traditional rulers first
aries mars
taurus venus
gemini mercury
cancer moon
leo sun
virgo mercury
libra venus
scorpio mars
sagittarius jupiter
capricorn saturn
aquarius saturn
pisces jupiter
this planet becomes the chart ruler

2 :- intermediate where the ruler is placed. check the house. this shows where life energy flows most strongly
example: aries rising with mars in 10th… life pushes toward ambition, recognition, visibility; same rising but mars in 12th… energy turns inward, hidden struggles, isolation patterns
check the sign. this shows how comfortable the planet is. mars in aries means direct, assertive. mars in cancer means reactive, emotional. this sets the tone of how life is handled

3 :- real strength dignity and house combined
essential dignity
domicile strongest
exaltation strong
detriment weak
fall weakest
accidental dignity house strength
angular 1 4 7 10 powerful
succedent 2 5 8 11 stable
cadent 3 6 9 12 weaker
real observation: strong house plus weak sign can still dominate life; strong sign plus weak house may struggle to show results

4 :- motion how the energy behaves

direct: outward, straightforward
retrograde: inward, reflective, sometimes delayed
stationary: very strong, almost intense

5 :- combustion interaction with the sun

under the suns beams around 17 degrees… reduced visibility
combust around 8 degrees… sun dominates
example: venus combust… relationships tied deeply with identity, sometimes burnout or validation issues; not always negative… sometimes it creates intensity

6 :- advanced dispositor chain

this is where hidden control shows up; every planet answers to another

example: mars in gemini goes to mercury; mercury in cancer goes to moon; moon in capricorn goes to saturn; final control saturn - so, even if mars is chart ruler, saturn may actually run the system

7 :- synthesis judging real strength

combine everything:

sign dignity
house placement
aspects
motion
combustion
dispositors

8 :- expert observations

sect day and night charts changes behavior
planet speed changes intensity
multiple rulership increases importance
timing techniques activate the ruler and trigger events

Prompt should call out these things when it sees it in a chart: 
Special focus on any planets in the first house
Chiron first house
Chiron conjunct any major planet: sun, moon, mars, Venus, mercury, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune, Pluto
Detriments: Mars in Libra, Venus in Aries, Mars in Taurus, Jupiter in Gemini, Saturn in Cancer, Saturn in Leo, Jupiter in Virgo, Venus in Scorpio, Mercury in Sagittarius, Moon in Capricorn, Sun in Aquarius, Pisces in Mercury
Any planets that sit on the ascendant 

Also consider: 
Who is the chart ruler and what this means for the overall chart
South node and North node and where personal growth should be focused based on this
part of fortune and part of spirit, and what comes naturally and what needs to be worked for
Descendant sign and what this means for how you show up in relationships
